msgstr "Trying 216.127.220.143...\nConnected to r47.bfm.org.\nEscape character is '^]'.\n2001-06-19T21:31:40Z\nConnection closed by foreign host.\n%\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:940
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"By the way, telnet prints the _Connection closed by foreign host_ message "
"after our daemon has closed the socket.  This shows us that, indeed, using "
"`fclose(client);` in our code works as advertised."
msgstr "顺便说一下，在我们的守护进程关闭套接字后，telnet 会打印 __Connection closed by foreign host__ 消息。这说明，在我们的代码中使用 `fclose(client);` 确实如预期那样有效。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:942
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Helper Functions"
msgstr "辅助函数"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:948
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"FreeBSD C library contains many helper functions for sockets programming.  "
"For example, in our sample client we hard coded the `time.nist.gov` IP "
"address.  But we do not always know the IP address.  Even if we do, our "
"software is more flexible if it allows the user to enter the IP address, or "
"even the domain name."
msgstr "FreeBSD C 库为套接字编程提供了许多辅助函数。例如，在示例客户端中，我们硬编码了 `time.nist.gov` 的 IP 地址。但我们并不总是知道 IP 地址。即使知道，如果软件允许用户输入 IP 地址，甚至域名，也会更加灵活。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:950
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`gethostbyname`"
msgstr "`gethostbyname`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:953
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"While there is no way to pass the domain name directly to any of the sockets "
"functions, the FreeBSD C library comes with the man:gethostbyname[3] and man:"
"gethostbyname2[3] functions, declared in [.filename]#netdb.h#."
msgstr "虽然无法将域名直接传递给任何套接字函数，但 FreeBSD C 库提供了 man:gethostbyname[3] 和 man:gethostbyname2[3] 函数，它们声明在 [.filename]#netdb.h# 中。"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:958
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"struct hostent * gethostbyname(const char *name);\n"
"struct hostent * gethostbyname2(const char *name, int af);\n"
msgstr "struct hostent * gethostbyname(const char *name);\nstruct hostent * gethostbyname2(const char *name, int af);\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:962
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Both return a pointer to the `hostent` structure, with much information "
"about the domain.  For our purposes, the `h_addr_list[0]` field of the "
"structure points at `h_length` bytes of the correct address, already stored "
"in the _network byte order_."
msgstr "两者都会返回一个指向 `hostent` 结构的指针，其中包含有关域名的大量信息。就我们的用途而言，该结构的 `h_addr_list[0]` 字段指向 `h_length` 个字节的正确地址，该地址已按__网络字节序__存储。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:964
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This allows us to create a much more flexible-and much more useful-version "
"of our daytime program:"
msgstr "这样，我们就能创建一个灵活得多、也实用得多的 daytime 程序："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:980
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"/*\n"
" * daytime.c\n"
" *\n"
" * Programmed by G. Adam Stanislav\n"
" * 19 June 2001\n"
" */\n"
"#include <stdio.h>\n"
"#include <string.h>\n"
"#include <unistd.h>\n"
"#include <sys/types.h>\n"
"#include <sys/socket.h>\n"
"#include <netinet/in.h>\n"
"#include <netdb.h>\n"
msgstr "/*\n * daytime.c\n *\n * Programmed by G. Adam Stanislav\n * 19 June 2001\n */\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <unistd.h>\n#include <sys/types.h>\n#include <sys/socket.h>\n#include <netinet/in.h>\n#include <netdb.h>\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:987
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"int main(int argc, char *argv[]) {\n"
"  int s, bytes;\n"
"  struct sockaddr_in sa;\n"
"  struct hostent *he;\n"
"  char buf[BUFSIZ+1];\n"
"  char *host;\n"
msgstr "int main(int argc, char *argv[]) {\n  int s, bytes;\n  struct sockaddr_in sa;\n  struct hostent *he;\n  char buf[BUFSIZ+1];\n  char *host;\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:997
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"  sa.sin_family = AF_INET;\n"
"  sa.sin_port = htons(13);\n"
msgstr "  sa.sin_family = AF_INET;\n  sa.sin_port = htons(13);\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:999
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "  host = (argc > 1) ? argv[1] : \"time.nist.gov\";\n"
msgstr "  host = (argc > 1) ? argv[1] : \"time.nist.gov\";\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:1004
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"  if ((he = gethostbyname(host)) == NULL) {\n"
"    herror(host);\n"
"    return 2;\n"
"  }\n"
msgstr "  if ((he = gethostbyname(host)) == NULL) {\n    herror(host);\n    return 2;\n  }\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:1006
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "  memcpy(&sa.sin_addr, he->h_addr_list[0], he->h_length);\n"
msgstr "  memcpy(&sa.sin_addr, he->h_addr_list[0], he->h_length);\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:1011
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"  if (connect(s, (struct sockaddr *)&sa, sizeof sa) < 0) {\n"
"    perror(\"connect\");\n"
"    return 3;\n"
"  }\n"
msgstr "  if (connect(s, (struct sockaddr *)&sa, sizeof sa) < 0) {\n    perror(\"connect\");\n    return 3;\n  }\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:1014
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"  while ((bytes = read(s, buf, BUFSIZ)) > 0)\n"
"    write(1, buf, bytes);\n"
msgstr "  while ((bytes = read(s, buf, BUFSIZ)) > 0)\n    write(1, buf, bytes);\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:1024
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"We now can type a domain name (or an IP address, it works both ways) on the "
"command line, and the program will try to connect to its _daytime_ server.  "
"Otherwise, it will still default to `time.nist.gov`.  However, even in this "
"case we will use `gethostbyname` rather than hard coding `132.163.96.1`.  "
"That way, even if its IP address changes in the future, we will still find "
"it."
msgstr "现在，我们可以在命令行中输入域名（或 IP 地址，两者都可以），程序会尝试连接到它的__daytime__服务器。否则，程序仍会默认使用 `time.nist.gov`。不过，即使在这种情况下，我们也会使用 `gethostbyname`，而不是硬编码 `132.163.96.1`。这样，即使它的 IP 地址将来发生变化，我们仍然能够找到它。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:1028
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Since it takes virtually no time to get the time from your local server, you "
"could run daytime twice in a row: First to get the time from `time.nist."
"gov`, the second time from your own system.  You can then compare the "
"results and see how exact your system clock is:"
msgstr "从本地服务器获取时间几乎不花时间，因此你可以连续运行两次 daytime：第一次从 `time.nist.gov` 获取时间，第二次从自己的系统获取。然后比较结果，就能查看系统时钟的精确程度："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:1032
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "% daytime ; daytime localhost\n"
msgstr "% daytime ; daytime localhost\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:1036
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"52080 01-06-20 04:02:33 50 0 0 390.2 UTC(NIST) *\n"
"2001-06-20T04:02:35Z\n"
"%\n"
msgstr "52080 01-06-20 04:02:33 50 0 0 390.2 UTC(NIST) *\n2001-06-20T04:02:35Z\n%\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:1039
#, fuzzy
msgid "As you can see, my system was two seconds ahead of the NIST time."
msgstr "如你所见，我的系统时间比 NIST 时间快了两秒。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:1041
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "`getservbyname`"
msgstr "`getservbyname`"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:1045
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Sometimes you may not be sure what port a certain service uses.  The man:"
"getservbyname[3] function, also declared in [.filename]#netdb.h# comes in "
"very handy in those cases:"
msgstr "有时你可能不确定某项服务使用哪个端口。这时，在 [.filename]#netdb.h# 中声明的 man:getservbyname[3] 函数就很有用："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:1049
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "struct servent * getservbyname(const char *name, const char *proto);\n"
msgstr "struct servent * getservbyname(const char *name, const char *proto);\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:1052
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The `servent` structure contains the `s_port`, which contains the proper "
"port, already in _network byte order_."
msgstr "`servent` 结构包含 `s_port` 字段，其中存储了正确的端口号，且已经按__网络字节序__排列。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:1054
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Had we not known the correct port for the _daytime_ service, we could have "
"found it this way:"
msgstr "如果我们不知道__daytime__服务使用的正确端口号，就可以这样查找："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:1064
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"struct servent *se;\n"
"  ...\n"
"  if ((se = getservbyname(\"daytime\", \"tcp\")) == NULL {\n"
"    fprintf(stderr, \"Cannot determine which port to use.\\n\");\n"
"    return 7;\n"
"  }\n"
"  sa.sin_port = se->s_port;\n"
msgstr "struct servent *se;\n  ...\n  if ((se = getservbyname(\"daytime\", \"tcp\")) == NULL {\n    fprintf(stderr, \"Cannot determine which port to use.\\n\");\n    return 7;\n  }\n  sa.sin_port = se->s_port;\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:1071
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You usually do know the port.  But if you are developing a new protocol, you "
"may be testing it on an unofficial port.  Some day, you will register the "
"protocol and its port (if nowhere else, at least in your [.filename]#/etc/"
"services#, which is where `getservbyname` looks).  Instead of returning an "
"error in the above code, you just use the temporary port number.  Once you "
"have listed the protocol in [.filename]#/etc/services#, your software will "
"find its port without you having to rewrite the code."
msgstr "通常你会知道端口号。但如果你正在开发新协议，可能会在非官方端口上测试它。将来，你会注册该协议及其端口（如果没有其他地方，至少会将其添加到 [.filename]#/etc/services# 中，`getservbyname` 会在这里查找）。此时，不必像上面的代码那样返回错误，只需使用临时端口号即可。将协议列入 [.filename]#/etc/services# 后，软件就能找到它的端口，无需你重新编写代码。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:1073
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Concurrent Servers"
msgstr "并发服务器"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:1077
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Unlike a sequential server, a _concurrent server_ has to be able to serve "
"more than one client at a time.  For example, a _chat server_ may be serving "
"a specific client for hours-it cannot wait till it stops serving a client "
"before it serves the next one."
msgstr "与顺序服务器不同，__并发服务器__必须能够同时为多个客户端提供服务。例如，__聊天服务器__可能需要为某个客户端服务数小时——它不能等到服务完一个客户端后才为下一个客户端服务。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:1079
#, fuzzy
msgid "This requires a significant change in our flowchart:"
msgstr "这需要对我们的流程图进行重大修改："

#. type: Block title
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:1080
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Concurrent Server"
msgstr "并发服务器"

#. type: Target for macro image
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:1081
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "serv2.png"
msgstr "serv2.png"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:1085
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"We moved the _serve_ from the _daemon process_ to its own _server process_.  "
"However, because each child process inherits all open files (and a socket is "
"treated just like a file), the new process inherits not only the _\"accepted "
"handle,\"_ i.e., the socket returned by the `accept` call, but also the _top "
"socket_, i.e., the one opened by the top process right at the beginning."
msgstr "我们将__服务__操作从__守护进程__移到了它自己的__服务器进程__中。不过，由于每个子进程都会继承所有打开的文件（而套接字也被视为文件），新进程不仅会继承__“已接受的句柄”__，也就是 `accept` 调用返回的套接字，还会继承__顶层套接字__，也就是顶层进程一开始打开的那个套接字。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:1088
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"However, the _server process_ does not need this socket and should `close` "
"it immediately.  Similarly, the _daemon process_ no longer needs the "
"_accepted socket_, and not only should, but _must_ `close` it-otherwise, it "
"will run out of available _file descriptors_ sooner or later."
msgstr "不过，__服务器进程__不需要这个套接字，应立即对其调用 `close`。同样，__守护进程__不再需要__已接受的套接字__，不仅应该，而且__必须__对其调用 `close`——否则迟早会耗尽可用的__文件描述符__。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:1091
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"After the _server process_ is done serving, it should close the _accepted "
"socket_.  Instead of returning to `accept`, it now exits."
msgstr "__服务器进程__完成服务后，应关闭__已接受的套接字__。它现在会直接退出，而不是返回 `accept`。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:1098
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Under UNIX(R), a process does not really _exit_.  Instead, it _returns_ to "
"its parent.  Typically, a parent process ``wait``s for its child process, "
"and obtains a return value.  However, our _daemon process_ cannot simply "
"stop and wait.  That would defeat the whole purpose of creating additional "
"processes.  But if it never does `wait`, its children will become _zombies_-"
"no longer functional but still roaming around."
msgstr "在 UNIX(R) 下，进程并不会真正__退出__，而是__返回__到父进程。通常，父进程会对其子进程执行 ``wait``，并获取返回值。不过，我们的__守护进程__不能简单地停下来等待，那样就违背了创建额外进程的初衷。但如果它从不执行 `wait`，其子进程就会变成__僵尸进程__——不再运行，却仍然留在系统中。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:1101
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"For that reason, the _daemon process_ needs to set _signal handlers_ in its "
"_initialize daemon_ phase.  At least a SIGCHLD signal has to be processed, "
"so the daemon can remove the zombie return values from the system and "
"release the system resources they are taking up."
msgstr "因此，__守护进程__需要在其__初始化守护进程__阶段设置信号处理程序。至少必须处理 SIGCHLD 信号，这样守护进程才能从系统中清除僵尸进程的返回值，并释放它们占用的系统资源。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/developers-handbook/sockets/_index.adoc:1104
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"That is why our flowchart now contains a _process signals_ box, which is not "
"connected to any other box.  By the way, many servers also process SIGHUP, "
"and typically interpret as the signal from the superuser that they should "
"reread their configuration files.  This allows us to change settings without "
"having to kill and restart these servers."
msgstr "这就是为什么我们的流程图现在包含一个__处理信号__框，它没有连接到任何其他框。顺便说一下，许多服务器也会处理 SIGHUP，通常将其解释为超级用户发出的信号，表示服务器应重新读取配置文件。这样，我们就可以更改设置，而无需终止并重新启动这些服务器。"
